[2026-11-25T22:42:00Z] note: setup: library spec (original.md + ../../EXECUTION.md, ../../INDICATORS.md), Yahoo daily adjusted bars. - In-sample (tuning): 1995-01-01 → 2016-01-01; out-of-sample (validation only): 2016-01-01 → 2026-11-23 (frozen end) - Each symbol trades only after 100 bars of its own history - Capital 10,000 USD, 100% of equity per trade, fractional units - Fees 0.05% per side, slippage 0.03% per fill Part of SHARD2 of the 120-spec library, split across parallel sessions; runs only while holding one of logs/tso-slot-{1,2,3}.lock (max 3 optimizer containers machine-wide).
[2026-11-25T22:42:00Z] note: assumptions: - Position size = 100% of equity per trade, not the spec's risk_fraction sizing (user's choice for the library, so results compare on the leaderboard); risk_fraction is therefore not optimized. - Costs: fee 0.05% per side, slippage 0.03% per fill (repo US ETF/stock defaults, library-wide convention), slightly above the spec's 5 bp scenario. - Fills on adjusted prices (the project has no separate raw execution series). - In-sample 1995-01-01 → 2016-01-01, out-of-sample 2016-01-01 → 2026-11-23 (repo precedent for ETF strategies; same split across the library). - Indicators: EMA/RMA seeded with the SMA of the first n values, ATR = Wilder RMA of TR (INDICATORS.md). - Screening universe: Yahoo ETFs (spec: ETF); listed instruments are alternatives, tested separately. - The spec has no tunable signal parameter: only the exits are optimized; EMA(10) is a fixed constant.
[2026-11-25T22:42:00Z] note: backtest.py adapted from template: strategy block = CONFIG/PARAMS/SPACE/valid/signals plus shared indicator helpers (SMA-seeded EMA/RMA, Wilder ATR, crosses, memo cache). _simulate extended (machinery change, needed by the spec): ATR(14) of the signal bar frozen at entry for stop = E - stop_atr*A and target = E + take_profit_atr*A, entry skipped if A<=0/NaN or stop<=0; max_candles used as the time exit (max_bars); after an intrabar stop/target exit the next signal may come from the following bar on; run() applies the entry veto buy & ~sell. Gap fills and stop-before-target as in the template.
[2026-11-25T22:42:00Z] note: sanity check: defaults in-sample: 4 trades, -0.39%/yr, max DD -9.0%, win 25.0%, median 3 bars, exits {'signal': 4}; out-of-sample: 2 trades, -0.39%/yr, max DD -4.8%, win 0.0%, median 10 bars, exits {'signal': 1, 'stop': 1}. Verified all 4 in-sample default trades against the raw bars (buy true and sell false on the signal bar, entry fill = next open + slippage, stop/target levels from the frozen signal-bar ATR and not touched earlier, signal exits after a sell bar, time exits at max_candles): 0 mismatches. Sample trade 2012-05-30 -> 2012-05-31 signal bars=1.
[2026-11-25T22:42:23Z] note: settings: defaults kept although the pattern is rare on the base symbol (defaults: double inside 4 IS trades on QQQ, hammer 8 on GLD). The base run may find nothing eligible; the broad basket over all screened symbols is where this strategy can gather enough trades. Not loosening the gates for a single symbol.
